<% content_for :title, "Model corpus discovery — NavishAI" %>
<% content_for :head do %><meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-preview"><% end %>
<main class="page-shell">
  <%= link_to @corpus.name, workspace_corpus_path(Current.workspace, @corpus), class: "back-link" %>
  <div class="page-heading"><div><h1>Model corpus discovery</h1><p>Company-specific families and source-backed candidates, not expert decisions.</p></div></div>
  <p><%= @batch ? "Bounded multi-request discovery sends every complete conversation, repeating all current documents in each discovery batch. At most one reducer receives validated proposals, not human labels or scenarios." : "One request sends the complete records shown below: titles, text and retained context." %> It can propose issue families, high-risk examples and scenario expectations. Quotes prove source links, not correctness. Taxonomy and scenarios still need expert review.</p>
  <p><%= @batch ? "At most 2000 complete records / 10 MiB, 30 discovery batches, each within 100 records / 256 KiB, and 20 final candidates." : "At most 100 conversation/document records, 256 KiB and 20 candidates." %> No silent sampling or truncation. Traces, existing scenarios and human labels stay local. Email masking is not full PII removal; review these records before disclosure.</p>
  <% if @model_input_error %>
    <p role="status" class="inline-error"><%= @model_input_error %></p><p>Add conversations or use a smaller corpus, then reopen this page. <%= link_to "Return to the corpus", workspace_corpus_path(Current.workspace, @corpus) %>. Local analysis also has complete-record limits.</p>
  <% else %>
    <div class="review-layout">
      <section aria-labelledby="disclosure-preview"><h2 id="disclosure-preview">Exact source preview</h2>
        <p><%= @model_items.size %> complete records · <%= number_to_human_size(@model_input.to_json.bytesize) %> · confirm again if sources change.</p>
        <% if @batch %>
          <h3>Exact allocation and maximum call plan</h3><p><%= @call_plan.fetch("batches").size %> discovery requests + <%= @call_plan.fetch("reducer") ? 1 : 0 %> reducer · maximum <%= @call_plan.fetch("maximum_calls") %> calls. Reducer accepts at most 200 intermediate clusters / 1 MiB; exceeding these stops the attempt without dropping proposals.</p>
          <p>Each batch has its own once-only UUID. Any abstention, error, interruption or changed authority stops later calls. Receipts cannot be mined until the whole analysis produces global proposals. No retry or crash continuation.</p>
          <details><summary>Fixed source digest and ordered record references</summary><pre class="evidence-text"><%= JSON.pretty_generate(@call_plan) %></pre></details>
          <details id="source-record-preview"><summary>Review all <%= @model_items.size %> exact source records</summary>
        <% end %>
        <% @model_items.each do |item| %>
          <details class="source-record"><summary><%= item.title %> · <%= item.source_snapshot.source.kind.humanize %></summary><p><%= link_to "Inspect source snapshot", source_evidence_path(item) %> · corpus-item-<%= item.id %></p><pre class="evidence-text"><%= item.content %></pre><h3>Retained context</h3><pre class="evidence-text"><%= JSON.pretty_generate(item.context) %></pre></details>
        <% end %>
        <% if @batch %></details><% end %>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="model-request"><h2 id="model-request">Request discovery</h2>
        <p>The operator must approve this exact workspace/endpoint in the separate corpus-processing registry. Target/judge or scenario-proposal approval cannot grant this disclosure. Each attempt claims once; unknown outcomes never retry.</p>
        <%= form_with url: workspace_corpus_corpus_analyses_path(Current.workspace, @corpus), class: "form-stack config-panel" do |form| %>
          <%= form.hidden_field :processing_method, value: @batch ? "model_batch" : "model" %><%= form.hidden_field :input_digest, value: ModelCorpusDiscovery.digest(@model_input) %>
          <% if @batch %><%= form.hidden_field :call_plan_digest, value: ModelCorpusDiscovery.digest(@call_plan) %><% end %>
          <div class="field"><%= form.label :scenario_limit, "Model candidate limit" %><%= form.number_field :scenario_limit, value: params[:scenario_limit].presence || 5, min: 1, max: 20, required: true %></div>
          <div class="field"><%= form.label :configuration, "Model configuration (JSON)" %><%= form.text_area :configuration, value: params[:configuration], rows: 6, maxlength: 10240, required: true, aria: { describedby: "model-config-help" } %><p id="model-config-help">Set endpoint, model and settings: temperature 0, max_output_tokens 256–4096, seed null or a non-negative integer. Never enter credentials.</p></div>
          <div class="checkbox-field"><%= form.check_box :corpus_disclose %><%= form.label :corpus_disclose, @batch ? "I approve these exact source records, repeated documents and the maximum call plan shown in the preview to the same endpoint, model and settings above." : "I approve sending these exact source records and retained context to the model endpoint above." %></div>
          <%= form.submit "Request model discovery", class: "button button-primary", data: { turbo_submits_with: "Queuing…" } %>
        <% end %>
      </section>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</main>
